> I am writing a recommendation letter for my PhD student. It includes a paragraph on the student's proposed project:
> ```
> Tahmid’s proposed project is a strong and timely extension of his broader research agenda on climate, agriculture, and welfare, which has focused on Bangladesh. The determinants of agricultural labor wages are of first-order importance in many lower-income countries, and Tahmid’s research recognizes the complex interactions between workers, farm owners, and field outcomes. He has already brought together multiple kinds of wage, yield, and environmental data, but it became clear during his PhD that a complete picture of these interactions would require a further series of projects. In particular, the proposal brings in a structured interview and survey process, to better understand the patterns he sees in the data. This information is relevant both to climate adaptation investment in Bangladesh and better understanding the risk of climate change and heat waves across the developing world. Labor productivity is one of the most economically significant impacts of climate change, but real-world evidence on it remains limited. In addition to the academic contribution, Tahmid’s work has the potential to feed directly into national-scale climate adaptation planning and labor interventions.
> ```
